docs/continuous-ingest-architecture.md:154:### `data/evidence/wiki_edit_audit.jsonl` — per-edit audit row (write barrier)
docs/continuous-ingest-architecture.md:274:- **OpenAI side:** the latest GPT-5.x slug available on AI Gateway at the moment the `dual-model-extractor` role is wired up. Recording happens at runtime — the resolved `model_slug` is written to every `model_extractions.jsonl` row, and the full `model_versions_used` list is written to every `wiki_edit_audit.jsonl` row.
docs/continuous-ingest-architecture.md:288:**No wiki edit lands without a matching row in `data/evidence/wiki_edit_audit.jsonl` in the same commit.**
docs/continuous-ingest-architecture.md:292:1. **Application-level.** Every worker that mutates a wiki page calls `recordEditOrAbort(edit)` exported from `tools/evidence/wiki-edit.ts`. If the worker does not call it, no file under `wiki/` is written.
docs/continuous-ingest-architecture.md:293:2. **Pre-commit hook.** `.husky/pre-commit` checks every commit. If the diff touches `wiki/**/*.md` and there is no matching diff in `data/evidence/wiki_edit_audit.jsonl`, the commit fails. This catches any code path that bypasses the helper.
docs/continuous-ingest-architecture.md:298:A defensibility report for any wiki page is a join from page sections → `wiki_edit_audit.jsonl` rows → `source_document` records. Output: a markdown report with every claim, every source backing it, retrieval date, models used, and model agreement state. Implemented as `npm run defensibility -- wiki/products/<page>.md`, extending `tools/audit-claim-provenance.mjs`.
docs/continuous-ingest-architecture.md:368:1. **Wiki edit semantics.** Both produce edits under `wiki/`. The continuous system's audit barrier applies only to its own edits (workers that call `recordEditOrAbort`). Nightly-orchestrator edits flow through the existing routing-audit and `log.md` paths. The pre-commit hook does not fail nightly commits because nightly does not touch the `wiki_edit_audit.jsonl` write path; backfill is explicitly out of scope.
docs/continuous-ingest-architecture.md:395:A defensibility report joins every numerical claim on a wiki page to its citation chain and the audit metadata in `wiki_edit_audit.jsonl`. It is the HMI-26 deliverable and the per-page query surface of the audit-row write barrier.

